<Base title="Work" description="Case studies and prototypes from 20+ years of product management in restaurant technology.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Featured work</p>
      <h1>Case studies & prototypes</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Projects that show how I approach product management in restaurant technology — from enterprise-scale
        deployments to team development programs — and the measurable results they delivered.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-top:3rem">
        <article class="case">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">Prototypes</p><h2>Restaurant Prototypes</h2></div>
          <div>
            <p>Working prototypes that address real restaurant problems, combining domain expertise with modern development to test market need and technical feasibility quickly.</p>
            <p>
              <strong>Smart Wing Pricing</strong> — two algorithmic approaches to pricing amid volatile commodity costs:
              <a href="https://wingpricer.netlify.app/">Version 1</a> and <a href="https://wingpricer2.netlify.app/">Version 2</a>.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Tax Compliance</strong> — tools for accurate restaurant tax calculation:
              <a href="https://taxscanner.netlify.app/">Scanner V1</a> and <a href="https://taxscanner.vercel.app/">Scanner V2</a>.
              The story behind them is in <a href="/blog/from-napkins-to-live-code-20-years-of-restaurant-tech-pain-points">From Napkins to Live Code</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="case">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">People</p><h2>PM Training & Certification</h2></div>
          <div>
            <p>Developed and delivered a training program that brought 15 product managers to Pragmatic Level IV certification, and led strategic offsites for vision alignment and roadmap planning across multiple product teams.</p>
            <p>Designed curriculum covering market-driven discovery, competitive positioning, and go-to-market execution, with measurable competency standards and certification pathways that became the company-wide PM development model.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="case">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">Operations</p><h2>Support Desk Transformation</h2></div>
          <div>
            <p>Turned around an underperforming support operation: average speed to answer went from 30+ minutes to under 30 seconds, mean time to resolve from 5+ weeks to 5 days, and every case older than 300 days was cleared.</p>
            <p>Redesigned processes, team structure, and performance tracking; created escalation protocols and a knowledge-management framework that raised first-call resolution. Customer satisfaction improved 99%, and the model was adopted company-wide.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="case">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">Delivery</p><h2>Enterprise POS Implementation</h2></div>
          <div>
            <p>Program-managed large-scale POS deployments, including the largest single-property MICROS implementation of its era — 300+ workstations at premier hospitality venues — coordinating operations, IT, and executive leadership.</p>
            <p>Managed complex integrations, stakeholder alignment, and zero-downtime cutovers for mission-critical restaurant operations. The deployment methodology and risk-mitigation standards became the template for future implementations.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
